. Cursor AI IDE
Cursor is an AI-powered code editor based on VS Code. It helps developers write, explain, modify, and debug code using AI.
Basic steps:
Install and open Cursor.
Create or open a project.
Write a prompt such as: “Create a responsive login page using HTML and CSS.”
Ask AI to generate or modify the code.
Review and test the generated code.
Use AI Chat to explain errors or improve the program.

Advantages of Cursor
AI-assisted code generation.
Can understand and work with project files.
Helps find and fix coding errors.
Provides code explanations.
Supports natural-language programming.
Useful for refactoring and improving existing code.
Familiar interface for VS Code users.

Disadvantages of Cursor
Some advanced AI features may require a paid plan.
AI-generated code can contain errors.
Requires internet access for many AI features.
Large projects can sometimes be difficult for AI to understand completely.
Users still need programming knowledge to verify AI output.

2. Replit AI IDE
Replit is a browser-based development environment that allows users to write, run, and share programs online. Its AI features can help create applications from natural-language instructions.

Advantages of Replit
Works directly in a web browser.
No complex local setup is required.
AI can help generate application code.
Easy to run and test programs.
Projects can be shared easily.
Supports many programming languages.
Useful for beginners and learning.

Disadvantages of Replit
Internet connection is generally required.
Some advanced features require paid plans.
AI-generated applications may need manual debugging.
Performance can depend on the online environment.
Free-plan resources and features may be limited.
